# Obsidian vault

## Gate

Use when the user asks to inventory, search, open, create, or edit notes in
an Obsidian vault (wikilinks, frontmatter, embeds, callouts). Skip ordinary
repo Markdown that is not under a resolved vault. Always load
`obsidian-safety` when delete/move/rename/bulk rewrite might appear.

Never invent a vault root, folder name, or note path. Resolve first.

## Resolve the vault

Before read/write, resolve the vault root from (in order):

1. Exact path the user named this turn
2. Workspace folder that contains `.obsidian/`
3. Connected MCP that lists vaults / notes (when ready)
4. Stop and ask once — do not guess a home-directory vault

Treat `.obsidian/` as app config: skip unless the user asked about
settings, plugins, or workspace JSON.

## Prefer MCP, else filesystem

When an Obsidian MCP is ready, prefer its inventory / read / write tools
over ad-hoc scans. If MCP is absent or incomplete, use the vault
filesystem under the resolved root — still never invent paths.

Do not invent MCP tool names. Discover the live tool list when connected;
fall back to list/search/read/write of `.md` files under the root.

## Inventory

1. List or search notes under the resolved root (title + relative path).
2. Prefer narrow search (folder, tag, filename substring) before dumping
   the whole vault tree.
3. Skip binary attachments unless the user asked about media embeds.
4. Report a short table or bullet list — not every file body.

## Author / edit notes

- **Body:** Obsidian-flavored Markdown (headings, lists, tables). Use
  callouts (`> [!note]`, `> [!warning]`, …) only when sibling notes already
  use them or the user asked.
- **Links inside the vault:** `[[Note]]`, `[[Note#Heading]]`,
  `[[Note|alias]]`, folder-qualified `[[folder/Note]]` when the vault uses
  that style.
- **Embeds:** `![[Note]]`, `![[image.png]]`, optional size
  `![[image.png|400]]` when peers already do.
- **Frontmatter:** valid YAML between `---` fences; preserve unknown keys;
  do not invent Dataview / Tasks / community-plugin fields unless already
  present in siblings or named by the user.
- Prefer updating the existing note over creating a near-duplicate title.
- Prefer edit-in-place; keep the user’s heading structure unless asked to
  restructure.

## Create

1. Confirm the target folder exists (or create only when the user asked).
2. Choose a title that does not collide with an existing note (search
   first).
3. Seed frontmatter only with keys the vault already uses (or the user
   named).
4. Receipt: relative path written.

## Tags and properties

- Inline tags (`#tag`) and frontmatter `tags:` — match vault convention
  (one style per vault; do not mix gratuitously).
- Do not mass-retag across folders (`obsidian-safety`).

## Report shape

- Vault root (short) + relative note path(s)
- What changed (created / edited / listed) — quote only a short excerpt
  when evidence is needed
- No full private journal dumps (`obsidian-safety`)

## Out of scope

- Memory-store export-to-Markdown tools (other products)
- Sync/publish/community plugin authoring unless the user named that
  surface and it lives in this vault’s `.obsidian/` with an explicit ask
- Site-specific absolute paths — resolve from the opened workspace
